WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:16.099
Unit fifteen: Object Pronouns (me/him/her). Today you will replace nouns after verbs with object pronouns.

4
00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:19.202
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.492
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.072
Me.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:28.083
Me means the object form of I.

8
00:00:28.683 --> 00:00:29.719
Please help me.

9
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:32.737
Your turn. Say: Me.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.555
Me.

11
00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:37.993
Him.

12
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:41.053
Him means the object form of he.

13
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:42.698
I know him.

14
00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:45.355
Your turn. Say: Him.

15
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:48.783
Him.

16
00:00:49.517 --> 00:00:50.320
Her.

17
00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.421
Her means the object form of she.

18
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:55.087
I like her.

19
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:57.860
Your turn. Say: Her.

20
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.272
Her.

21
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:02.867
Us.

22
00:01:03.883 --> 00:01:05.767
Us means the object form of we.

23
00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:07.628
She teaches us.

24
00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:10.172
Your turn. Say: Us.

25
00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:13.779
Us.

26
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:15.123
Them.

27
00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:18.209
Them means the object form of they.

28
00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:19.760
I see them.

29
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.352
Your turn. Say: Them.

30
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:25.888
Them.

31
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.280
It.

32
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:30.840
It means the form for a thing or an animal.

33
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.381
I love it.

34
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:35.136
Your turn. Say: It.

35
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:38.560
It.

36
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:40.167
Subject.

37
00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:44.135
Subject means the person or thing that does the action.

38
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.436
In 'I eat', I is the subject.

39
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.261
Your turn. Say: Subject.

40
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.124
Subject.

41
00:01:53.883 --> 00:01:54.768
Object.

42
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:58.874
Object means the person or thing that receives the action.

43
00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:01.367
In 'help me', me is the object.

44
00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:04.369
Your turn. Say: Object.

45
00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:08.292
Object.

46
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.716
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.513
Visal, do we say 'She helps I' or 'She helps me'?

48
00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:28.991
We say 'She helps me'. After a verb, we use an object pronoun. I becomes me, he becomes him, she becomes her, we becomes us, they becomes them.

49
00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.154
What does 'it' do?

50
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:40.129
It stays the same: I love it. It is both a subject and an object pronoun. You also stays the same: I see you.

51
00:02:41.217 --> 00:02:43.356
Where do the object pronouns go?

52
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:54.515
After a verb or a preposition: I like him. She talks to us. Look at them. They help us avoid repeating a noun, so the sentence sounds natural.

53
00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.492
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:04.355
Grammar focus: Object pronouns: me and you and him and her and it and us and them.

55
00:03:04.655 --> 00:03:05.795
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:08.030
She helps me every day.

57
00:03:08.917 --> 00:03:10.371
I know him very well.

58
00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:13.097
The teacher teaches us English.

59
00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:22.049
Use object pronouns after a verb or a preposition: me, you, him, her, it, us, them. Do not use I, he, she, we or they there.

60
00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:26.306
Be careful! Don't say: She helps I every day.

61
00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.359
Say: She helps me every day.

62
00:03:30.659 --> 00:03:33.309
Use me, not I, after the verb.

63
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.648
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.433 --> 00:03:38.829
Using Pronouns.

65
00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:41.663
I have two friends, and I see them every day.

66
00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:45.258
My teacher is kind, so we like her.

67
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.847
My brother is funny, and everybody loves him.

68
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:51.949
My mother calls me when dinner is ready.

69
00:03:52.933 --> 00:03:55.746
A pronoun saves us from repeating the same noun.

70
00:03:56.833 --> 00:04:00.893
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.693
I like Tom. I see blank every day.

72
00:04:04.993 --> 00:04:08.019
A, he. B, him. C, his.

73
00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.485
The answer is B: him.

74
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.733
The teacher helps blank. (we)

75
00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:19.909
A, we. B, our. C, us.

76
00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.420
The answer is C: us.

77
00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:28.911
Look at the girls. Do you know blank?

78
00:04:29.211 --> 00:04:32.040
A, them. B, they. C, their.

79
00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.333
The answer is A: them.

80
00:04:38.483 --> 00:04:40.123
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:40.423 --> 00:04:44.982
A, She loves I.. B, She loves me.. C, She loves my..

82
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:50.777
The answer is B: She loves me..

83
00:04:51.917 --> 00:04:55.008
According to the reading, who calls the writer when dinner is ready?

84
00:04:55.308 --> 00:04:58.926
A, my mother. B, my brother. C, my teacher.

85
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.710
The answer is A: my mother.

86
00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:09.052
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:12.323
Write a sentence using the object pronoun 'them'.

88
00:05:21.117 --> 00:05:22.559
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:22.859 --> 00:05:36.636
I see my grandparents every Sunday, and I help them in the garden. I use them because it replaces my grandparents. Object pronouns like me, him, her, us and them come after the verb.

90
00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.692
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:39.583 --> 00:05:46.555
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and object pronouns: me and you and him and her and it and us and them.

92
00:05:46.855 --> 00:05:50.610
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

93
00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.632
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:53.932 --> 00:05:57.339
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

